{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesjuuGgJnWUjPLL4hpZ5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## ANALYSIS\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED status (idempotently), rejects CANCELLED shipments with HTTP 409, and returns HTTP 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — defines `ShipmentStatus` enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — defines `Shipment` data class with mutable `status` field\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — existing `create()` endpoint creates shipments in CREATED status\n- `ShipmentController.kt:46-52` — existing `getById()` endpoint shows how to throw `ResourceNotFoundException`\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18` — `save()` method persists changes to existing shipments\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — defines `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — defines `ErrorCode` enum (I will need to add a new code for invalid state)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — automatically converts exceptions to HTTP responses with proper status codes\n- No existing endpoint performs state transitions; CONFIRMED and CANCELLED are unreachable today\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Error handling: throw `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404, `ConflictException` for 409\n- Error codes: defined in `ErrorCode` enum; each failure case gets its own code\n- Return types: controllers return bare entities for GET (status 200), `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body()` for POST with 201\n- Tests: use `MockMvc` with `post()` and `get()` builders, assert both status and `jsonPath` of response body\n- Tests check error response shape via `$.error.code` and `$.error.message` paths\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code (required: error contract must list all possible codes)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — add `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` endpoint (required: implements the feature)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for confirm, retry, cancelled state, missing shipment (required: cover all cases the ticket names)\n\n**Risks:**\n- If the idempotent retry case is not implemented, the endpoint breaks the requirement\n- If error codes are not exhaustive, future callers cannot distinguish between error types\n- If I accidentally modify repository behavior or entity structure, existing tests may break\n- The shipment status is immutable in the data class; I need to handle that correctly with `copy()`\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone. The ticket clearly specifies: transition CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent on CONFIRMED, 409 on CANCELLED, 404 on missing. The only design choice is the error code name for the CANCELLED rejection, which I will call `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to indicate the state prevents confirmation.\n\n---\n\n## DESIGN\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This code indicates the shipment is in a state (CANCELLED) that prevents confirmation.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`**: Add a new endpoint:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   This endpoint:\n   - Finds the shipment; throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if missing\n   - If status is CREATED, saves it with status CONFIRMED and returns it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM`\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`**: Add tests:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and returns 200` — POST to confirm, expect OK and CONFIRMED status\n   - `is idempotent: confirming an already-confirmed shipment succeeds` — confirm twice, both succeed\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` — reject with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n   - `rejects confirming a missing shipment with 404` — reject with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered adding a service layer (e.g., `ShipmentService`) to hold the confirm logic, but the existing controllers already have their own logic (e.g., the `create()` method calls `repository.save()` directly). Adding a service layer would be scope creep (\"unrelated refactoring\") and would break the pattern already established. The controller directly accesses the repository.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | findById(id) | save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200 OK + Shipment | Normal return |\n| Already CONFIRMED | findById(id) | none | 200 OK + Shipment | Normal return (no write) |\n| CANCELLED | findById(id) | none | 409 Conflict + error envelope | Throw ConflictException |\n| Missing | findById(id) returns null | none | 404 Not Found + error envelope | Throw ResourceNotFoundException |\n\nAll exceptions are caught by `GlobalExceptionHandler`, which returns the proper HTTP status and error envelope.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1** — `confirms a created shipment` — Create S-1, confirm it, assert 200, status CONFIRMED, shipmentId preserved\n- **Test 2** — `is idempotent` — Create S-2, confirm twice, both return 200 with CONFIRMED status, repository has only one entry\n- **Test 3** — `rejects cancelled shipment` — Directly save CANCELLED shipment to repository, confirm it, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n- **Test 4** — `rejects missing shipment` — Confirm unknown ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION\n\nNow I'll write the code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":452,"cache_read_input_tokens":18568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":452},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07e9cefa-33f4-4669-b931-6db022787e9f","uuid":"46ec69c9-fe27-4c2a-af43-9bbfb9ea44b3","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:53:41.946Z","request_id":"req_011CesjutcEiUwCebNWf85j9"}
